[38] Neither party has proposed a serious question of general importance for certification, and I am satisfied that none arises on the particular facts of this case (Canada (Minister of Citizenship and Immigration) v Liyanagamage, [1994] FCJ No 1637 at para 4).
JUDGMENT
THIS COURT’S JUDGMENT is that:
1. The application for judicial review is allowed;
2. The RAD decision is set aside;
3. The matter is referred back to the RAD for re-consideration of admissibility of the new evidence and re-determination on the merits by a differently constituted panel;
4. No serious question of general importance is certified for appeal.
"Denis Gascon"
Judge
FEDERAL COURT
